      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>I've done some testing to compare LevelDB and MySQL persistence performance:</p>\n\n<p><a href=\"https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA4x/MySQL+vs.+LevelDB+Performance\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">https://wiki.duraspace.org/display/FEDORA4x/MySQL+vs.+LevelDB+Performance</a></p>\n\n<p>The summary is that they are pretty similar, except that using the default auto-generated identifiers, listing objects in MySQL slowed down more quickly than it does with LevelDB.</p>",
     "created": "17/Feb/16 2:48 PM",
     "id": "16155",
     "jsdPublic": true,
     "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/11838/comment/16155",
